example

# generated native folders
/ios
/android
# The `google-services.json` under `android/app/` is generated with them. The copy
# at the repo root is tracked deliberately: EAS builds from a git archive, so an
# ignored file never reaches the build server, and Android push would lose its
# configuration on cloud builds while working on the machine that made them.

# local agent scratch
.claude/

.env*
# ...but the template is the only documentation of what has to be set.
!.env.example
